module nfkbLocalizationDetection
module tnfSecretionDetection

manifest RAW2647_Macrophages
manifest PluronicF127
manifest PBS
manifest CultureMedium
manifest LPS_500ngmL
manifest TNF_CaptureBeads
manifest TNF_DetectionAntibody
manifest SecondaryFluorescentAntibody
manifest PBSTween

instructions:

// ============================================================
// High-Content Quantification of Single-Cell Immune Dynamics
// Junkin, Kaestli, Cheng, Jordi, Albayrak, Hoffmann, Tay
// Cell Reports 15, 411-422, April 2016
// DOI: 10.1016/j.celrep.2016.03.033
//
// Platform: two-layer PDMS microfluidic chip (Melin & Quake
// design). 40 individually addressable 1.35 nL isolated cell
// chambers. Membrane valves and on-chip peristaltic pumps
// control all fluid routing. Mounted on automated inverted
// epifluorescence microscope (Nikon Eclipse Ti) inside
// atmospheric enclosure (37 C, 5% CO2, saturating humidity).
//
// Cells: RAW 264.7 mouse macrophages. Non-adherent; retained
// by weir-type trap (slits without bypass) inside chambers
// functionalized to be non-adherent (Pluronic F-127 coated).
//
// Stimulation: LPS (Sigma L4524) 500 ng/mL, single 2 hr
// pulse (Fig 4B left; mimics brief pathogen exposure).
// Input switching time < 5 s via 16-inlet binary multiplexer.
//
// Readout 1 -- TNF secretion bead immunoassay (dynamic):
//   Antibody-functionalized beads (Spherotech SVP-100-4,
//   10.3 um streptavidin, biotinylated capture Ab) pre-loaded
//   in 7 bead storage chambers per column. Every 2 hr, the
//   peristaltic pump transfers medium from cell chamber to
//   binding chamber; beads circularly mixed for 90 min.
//   After binding, beads rinsed with PBS-Tween and returned
//   to storage. At run end, detection Ab + secondary Ab
//   complete the sandwich; beads imaged; intensity correlated
//   to on-chip calibration curve (R2 = 0.9984, Fig 2B).
//   LOD: ~60,000 TNF molecules. 7 time windows: 0-2, 2-4,
//   4-6, 6-8, 8-10, 10-12, 12-14 hr post-stimulus.
//
// Readout 2 -- NF-kB (RelA) localization (dynamic):
//   Time-lapse epifluorescence imaging every ~6 min.
//   Cells express RelA-GFP; nuclear/cytoplasmic ratio
//   reports NF-kB activation state continuously.
//
// BioScript abstraction notes:
//   - `mix` is a consuming operation on both operands.
//     The "cell thread" is modelled as a fluid variable
//     that is re-produced at every feeding or sampling step
//     by mixing with the incoming fresh medium or bead-wash
//     product. This reflects how peristaltic pumping cycles
//     fluid through and out of the cell chamber.
//   - `mix cellVar with LPS_500ngmL` abstracts multiplexer
//     routing of the LPS inlet into the chamber for 2 hr.
//   - `heat` at 37c models on-chip incubation (non-consuming).
//   - Bead time-points: each window uses a freshly dispensed
//     bead variable; the washed bead product carries into the
//     next step as the cell-thread carrier, maintaining a
//     single linear ownership chain through the experiment.
//   - `detect nfkbLocalizationDetection` abstracts nuclear
//     RelA ratio measurement; consumes the cell variable.
//   - `detect tnfSecretionDetection` abstracts bead
//     fluorescence + calibration curve lookup (baseline
//     bead used as QC gate key; returns > 0 if any bead
//     window exceeds LOD of ~60,000 TNF molecules).
//   - h token unsupported: 2 hr = 120m throughout.
//   - `dispose` in pass-branches; `drain` in fail-branches.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main           -- chip prep, cell loading, baseline
//                          TNF assay (t0), LPS 2 hr pulse,
//                          6x post-stimulus TNF assays,
//                          sandwich Ab completion, NF-kB detect
//   BB2  nfkbPass       -- nfkbSignal > 0: RelA nuclear peak
//                          detected; dispose cell variable
//   BB3  nfkbFail       -- nfkbSignal <= 0: no activation;
//                          drain cell variable
//   BB4  nfkbJoin       -- join: TNF QC gate follows
//   BB5  tnfPass        -- tnfSignal > 0: TNF detected;
//                          dispose baseline bead variable
//   BB6  tnfFail        -- tnfSignal <= 0: all beads below
//                          LOD; drain baseline bead variable
//   BB7  finalCleanup   -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Chip surface preparation.
//   All internal surfaces except cell chambers coated with
//   2 mg/mL Pluronic F-127 in DI water overnight via control
//   script to block protein adsorption and bead adhesion.
//   Rinsed extensively with PBS before cell loading.
//   `mix` abstracts the automated overnight rinse sequence.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pluronicSol  = dispense 1 units of PluronicF127
pbsRinse     = dispense 1 units of PBS
devicePrimed = mix pluronicSol with pbsRinse for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Cell loading.
//   RAW 264.7 macrophages (versene-detached, 20 um filtered,
//   1e5-3.5e5 cells/mL) flowed through inlets. Binary
//   multiplexer directs cells to individual chambers. Weir
//   trap captures non-adherent macrophages. < 10 min total.
//   `mix` abstracts the flow-through trapping event.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

macrophages  = dispense 1 units of RAW2647_Macrophages
cellsLoaded  = mix macrophages with devicePrimed for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Post-loading equilibration.
//   Fresh medium pumped into chamber; cells equilibrate
//   inside sealed chambers at 37 C / 5% CO2 for 2 hr.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medEq        = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
cellsEq      = mix cellsLoaded with medEq for 10m
heat cellsEq at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Baseline TNF bead capture (t = 0-2 hr, pre-LPS).
//   Medium surrounding cells sampled for 2 hr to establish
//   pre-stimulus TNF baseline. Bead_1 transferred from
//   storage to binding chamber; medium + bead mixed by
//   circular peristaltic pumping for 90 min (Fig 2A).
//   Bead rinsed with PBS-Tween; returned to storage.
//   `mix cellsEq with medT0` models the medium sampling
//   step (consumes cellsEq); bead1Washed carries the
//   cell-thread forward into the stimulation phase.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medT0        = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleT0     = mix cellsEq with medT0 for 120m

bead1        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt1         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead1Bound   = mix sampleT0 with bead1 for 90m
bead1Washed  = mix bead1Bound with pbt1 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: LPS stimulation -- 2 hr pulse.
//   LPS at 500 ng/mL injected via multiplexer into cell
//   chamber for exactly 2 hr. Switching time < 5 s.
//   `mix bead1Washed with lpsInput` abstracts the LPS
//   inlet routing; bead1Washed carries the cell state
//   as fluid thread; result is cellsStim.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsInput     = dispense 1 units of LPS_500ngmL
cellsStim    = mix bead1Washed with lpsInput for 120m
heat cellsStim at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: LPS washout.
//   Multiplexer switches back to medium inlet; LPS-free
//   medium flows through chamber (< 5 s switchover time).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medWash      = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
cellsWashed  = mix cellsStim with medWash for 10m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: TNF bead capture -- time point 1 (0-2 hr post-LPS).
//   Medium sampled from chamber; bead_2 moved to binding
//   chamber and mixed for 90 min; rinsed with PBS-Tween.
//   bead2Washed carries cell thread into next window.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP1       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP1    = mix cellsWashed with medTP1 for 120m

bead2        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt2         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead2Bound   = mix sampleTP1 with bead2 for 90m
bead2Washed  = mix bead2Bound with pbt2 for 5m

heat bead2Washed at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: TNF bead capture -- time point 2 (2-4 hr post-LPS).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP2       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP2    = mix bead2Washed with medTP2 for 120m

bead3        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt3         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead3Bound   = mix sampleTP2 with bead3 for 90m
bead3Washed  = mix bead3Bound with pbt3 for 5m

heat bead3Washed at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: TNF bead capture -- time point 3 (4-6 hr post-LPS).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP3       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP3    = mix bead3Washed with medTP3 for 120m

bead4        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt4         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead4Bound   = mix sampleTP3 with bead4 for 90m
bead4Washed  = mix bead4Bound with pbt4 for 5m

heat bead4Washed at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: TNF bead capture -- time point 4 (6-8 hr post-LPS).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP4       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP4    = mix bead4Washed with medTP4 for 120m

bead5        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt5         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead5Bound   = mix sampleTP4 with bead5 for 90m
bead5Washed  = mix bead5Bound with pbt5 for 5m

heat bead5Washed at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 11: TNF bead capture -- time point 5 (8-10 hr post-LPS).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP5       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP5    = mix bead5Washed with medTP5 for 120m

bead6        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt6         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead6Bound   = mix sampleTP5 with bead6 for 90m
bead6Washed  = mix bead6Bound with pbt6 for 5m

heat bead6Washed at 37c for 120m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 12: TNF bead capture -- time point 6 (10-12 hr post-LPS).
//   Final medium sampling window. bead7Washed carries the
//   cell-thread terminal state into the sandwich completion.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

medTP6       = dispense 1 units of CultureMedium
sampleTP6    = mix bead6Washed with medTP6 for 120m

bead7        = dispense 1 units of TNF_CaptureBeads
pbt7         = dispense 1 units of PBSTween
bead7Bound   = mix sampleTP6 with bead7 for 90m
bead7Washed  = mix bead7Bound with pbt7 for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Sandwich assay completion -- detection antibodies.
//   After all 7 time-point bead captures, detection Ab
//   (genwaybio GWB-489500, 3.19 ug/mL) applied for 30 min
//   with circular mixing, then secondary fluorescent Ab
//   (USB I1903-12H, 3.3 ug/mL) for 30 min. PBS-Tween rinse
//   between steps. bead7Washed carries the accumulated
//   cell-state thread; `mix` with detAb and secAb models
//   the Ab incubation over all stored beads simultaneously.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

detAb        = dispense 1 units of TNF_DetectionAntibody
secAb        = dispense 1 units of SecondaryFluorescentAntibody

detStep      = mix bead7Washed with detAb for 30m
sandwichDone = mix detStep with secAb for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 14: NF-kB (RelA) localization -- aggregate QC readout.
//   Automated stage images every ~6 min throughout the 20 hr
//   run in GFP and brightfield channels. RelA-GFP nuclear/
//   cytoplasmic ratio computed per frame by MATLAB. Here,
//   nfkbLocalizationDetection abstracts the binary
//   determination: was a RelA nuclear peak observed (> 2 SD
//   above pre-stimulus baseline) during or after LPS pulse?
//   ~93.6% of cells (n=46) show NF-kB activation peak
//   following LPS stimulation (Fig 6A).
//   `detect` is applied to sandwichDone which holds the
//   terminal cell state; this consumes sandwichDone.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

nfkbSignal   = detect nfkbLocalizationDetection on sandwichDone for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: NF-kB activation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): nfkbSignal > 0 -> RelA nuclear peak detected;
//             cell categorised NF-kB+; dispose sandwichDone.
// Fail (BB3): nfkbSignal <= 0 -> no activation peak;
//             cell categorised NF-kB-; drain sandwichDone.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (nfkbJoin).
// ============================================================

if (nfkbSignal > 0) {
    dispose sandwichDone
} else {
    drain sandwichDone
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: nfkbJoin
// Dispose NF-kB QC signal. Control falls into TNF
// secretion QC gate (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose nfkbSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 15: TNF secretion fluorescence readout.
//   Beads in storage chambers imaged (brightfield + GFP
//   channel). Fluorescence correlated to on-chip calibration
//   curve (R2 = 0.9984, LOD ~60,000 molecules, Fig 2B).
//   tnfSecretionDetection applied to bead1Washed (baseline
//   bead, still alive from STEP 4) as the QC gate key;
//   signal > 0 if any time-point bead exceeds LOD.
//   ~93.5% of cells produce detectable TNF (Fig 6A).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfSignal    = detect tnfSecretionDetection on bead1Washed for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: TNF secretion QC gate
// Pass (BB5): tnfSignal > 0 -> measurable TNF secretion in
//             at least one 2 hr window (TNF+ cell);
//             dispose bead1Washed.
// Fail (BB6): tnfSignal <= 0 -> all time-point beads below
//             LOD (TNF- cell, ~6.5% per Fig 6A); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (tnfSignal > 0) {
    dispose bead1Washed
} else {
    drain bead1Washed
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose TNF QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose tnfSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
